ould shift to Candidate C because of reliability and positive crew atmosphere, despite communication difficulty.\n\nShe should incorporate D's info: arrogance, weak leadership, moody, loner. That suggests D is not good for crew cooperation. So D likely not candidate.\n\nShe may also ask about Candidate A's reliability and stress handling. But maybe she can argue that B remains best, but we need more info on A's reliability and stress. She could ask James for that.\n\nThus Emily's public message: She acknowledges D's attitude concerns, says that despite D's problem solving and responsibility, his poor crew cooperation makes him less suitable than B. She may still keep vote for B, but note that we still need to discuss A's reliability and stress handling. She may ask James for evidence on A.\n\nThus vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
